  "notes": "Online-only program delivered through Penn State World Campus in collaboration with multiple colleges. New catalogs created: dart_catalog.json (DART 100/202), dmd_catalog.json (DMD 100/300/400); extended comm_catalog.json with COMM 215/230W and art_catalog.json with ART 211Y. Real bug found: COMM 230W's actual prereq is ENGL 15 AND ENGL 202, but the bulletin's own suggested plan schedules COMM 230W in Semester 2 -- long before ENGL 202 appears in Semester 5. Left COMM 230W in its bulletin-labeled Semester 2 slot (for readability against the source) and let the simulator naturally defer it to whichever real term follows ENGL 202's completion, the same 'engine reorders across mislabeled bulletin semesters automatically' behavior already relied on for Graphic Design's GD 495. DMD 300's own 'any 9 credits from a 6-course list' sub-prereq isn't modeled literally (schema only supports simple OR-groups), but the plan schedules 5 of those 6 courses in Semesters 1-3, so it's always satisfied in practice by DMD 300's Semester 7 placement -- documented in dmd_catalog.json rather than silently ignored. 'Supporting Course for Major' (18cr, matches exactly: 6cr 'history of art/design/technology/communications' + 12cr 'related' World Campus coursework, both genuinely 'in consultation with an adviser' with no closed list) is modeled generically, same convention as CMPSC's own open pools. 2026-08-27 re-verification against the live bulletin's own Suggested Academic Plan tab HTML (DOM-extracted directly): (1) fixed a note-text error -- the real footnote states Additional Courses total 27cr, not 30cr as previously written here (the plan's 9 generic slots at 3cr each already correctly summed to 27); (2) found DMD 400 modeled at 6cr when the real bulletin has it at 3cr, paired with FOUR 'General Education Course' items in Fourth Year Spring (this plan only had three) -- fixed the credit value and added the missing 4th GEN ED slot; (3) the bulletin's own footnote 1 names a real, closed 44-course list for 'Additional Course for Major' (AA 121; ART 1/10/20/30/122Y; COMM 118/130/180/210/262/280/282/296/310(=IST 310)/342W/346/428A/492/493/495/496; DART 203/204/205/206/296/297/300/303/412/495/496/497; GD 110/210; HCDD 264/311/361; IST 140/240/256/261/402) -- previously mismodeled as a fully generic, unfillable placeholder despite this closed list existing; wired all 9 occurrences to it (added AA and GD to `departments`), excluding DART 100 from the pool since it's already a separate required Semester 2 item (including it caused the exact same recommend-the-same-course-forever deadlock found and fixed in the Digital Arts and Media Design build).",
